# SQL's `project *` alone: DS0117 with a fix that removes the step.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | project * | take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..34
  PIPELINE@0..33
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    PROJECT_OP@15..24
      IDENT@15..22 "project"
      WHITESPACE@22..23 " "
      ERROR@23..24
        STAR@23..24 "*"
    WHITESPACE@24..25 " "
    PIPE@25..26 "|"
    WHITESPACE@26..27 " "
    TAKE_OP@27..33
      IDENT@27..31 "take"
      WHITESPACE@31..32 " "
      LITERAL@32..33
        LONG@32..33 "5"
  WHITESPACE@33..34 "\n"

error[DS0117]: `project *` is SQL's `SELECT *`
  --> query:1:24
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | project * | take 5
  |                        ^ `project` lists the columns to keep
  |
  = help: every column is kept already: remove `| project *`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | take 5
which parses without errors
